Third-party components
----------------------

This source distribution contains no vendored third-party source. Its direct
external dependencies are resolved from the crate registry at build time:

  sha2 (RustCrypto)   Apache-2.0 OR MIT
                      Used by musubi-core for the content digest over the
                      canonical bytes of an Evidence envelope. Pure computation:
                      it performs no input or output of any kind, which is why a
                      crate that must have no network in its closure can depend
                      on it.

  serde              Apache-2.0 OR MIT
  serde_json         Apache-2.0 OR MIT
                      Used by musubi-jsonl-log for offline decoded JSON records.
                      No external binary-log decoder is included or invoked.

The remaining entries in the lockfile are these crates' transitive
dependencies. Their licences and their exact versions are recorded in Cargo.lock
and are checked by the cargo-deny policy in deny.toml on every CI run.
